==== Opening the case ====

**Note:** This will void your warranty! Be careful not to pull on any of the cables!

  - Pop the top cover by using small amount of force
  - Remove 4 screws holding the outer case from the top side and remove the outer case
  - Remove 4 screws holding the inner cover
  - Remove the inner cover. At this point the PCB is visible together with the console header, likely no need to proceed further. 
  - Remove the bottom sticker and the 4 screws behind it and remove the bottom cover (if desired)
  - Remove the PCB from the plastic chassis by releasing it from the 4 plastic tabs that hold it

